.TH ESDM\-SERVER\-SIGNAL\-HELPER 8 "2026-08-05" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
esdm\-server\-signal\-helper \- notify the ESDM server about suspend and resume
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esdm\-server\-signal\-helper
.B \-\-suspend
.B \-\-pid
.I PIDFILE
.br
.B esdm\-server\-signal\-helper
.B \-\-resume
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esdm\-server\-signal\-helper
tells a running
.BR esdm\-server (8)
that the system is about to be suspended, and that it has resumed.
.PP
On
.BR \-\-suspend ,
the helper reads the PID of the daemon from its PID file and, if that process
holds the lock of the file, sends it
.BR SIGUSR1 .
The daemon then marks itself as suspended in the status shared memory segment,
so that consumers waiting on it do not block on a daemon that is about to stop
running.
.PP
On
.BR \-\-resume ,
the helper connects to the privileged RPC interface and forces a reseed of the
DRNGs
.RB ( esdm_rpcc_rnd_reseed_crng (),
see
.BR libesdm_rpc_client (3)),
as
.B esdm\-tool \-\-reseed\-crng
does. This requires root; no PID file is needed for it.
.PP
Both operations are wired to the sleep targets by the shipped
.BR esdm\-server\-suspend.service " and " esdm\-server\-resume.service
systemd units, so the helper rarely needs to be invoked by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-suspend
Signal the impending suspend. Requires
.BR \-\-pid .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-resume
Signal the completed resume. Requires root. Ignored when given together with
.BR \-\-suspend .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pid " \fIPIDFILE\fR"
Read the PID of the daemon from
.IR PIDFILE .
Required by
.BR \-\-suspend ,
not used by
.BR \-\-resume .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit with a non\-zero status.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 when the requested notification was delivered, and a non\-zero status
otherwise \- including when no mode was requested at all, when
.B \-\-suspend
is given without
.B \-\-pid
or the PID file names no running server, and when
.B \-\-resume
is run by another user than root.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/esdm\-server.pid
PID file written by
.BR esdm\-server (8)
when started with
.BR \-\-pid ,
and the file the shipped suspend unit passes to this helper.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esdm\-server (8),
.BR esdm\-tool (1),
.BR libesdm_rpc_client (3)
.SH AUTHOR
Stephan Mueller <smueller@chronox.de>
